# THIRD PARTY NOTICES

This project is designed as a browser-based educational lab and uses a mix of original implementation plus external references described in the project specification. The following notices are included to document the expected open-source references and to make integration status explicit.

## 1. Core runtime and tooling

- Name: React
- Author: Meta Platforms, Inc.
- Repository: https://github.com/facebook/react
- License: MIT
- Usage: UI framework for the application shell and modular experiment workspace.
- Status: Verified for local development and production build.

- Name: Vite
- Author: Vite Contributors
- Repository: https://github.com/vitejs/vite
- License: MIT
- Usage: Build tool and dev server.
- Status: Verified for local development and production build.

## 2. Educational references from the specification

The following open-source repositories were used as conceptual references while creating the architecture and module taxonomy. They were not copied wholesale into this repository without review.

- Neural Sandbox — https://github.com/yushuosun/neural-sandbox
- TensorFlow Playground — https://github.com/tensorflow/playground
- TensorFlow.js Examples — https://github.com/tensorflow/tfjs-examples
- NN Playground — https://github.com/deBilla/nn-playground
- Pathfinding Playground — https://github.com/AlfaKBravo/Pathfinding-Playground
- Murmur Boids — https://github.com/ctkrug/murmur
- Digit Recognition TensorFlow.js — https://github.com/CarlosJChileS/digit-recognition-tfjs
- Neural Network Evolution — https://github.com/kibotu/NeuralNetworkEvolution
- DSA Visualizer — https://github.com/Mohit211205/DSA-Visualizer
- VisualML — https://github.com/dsgiitr/VisualML

License status for each repository must be checked before direct code reuse. This scaffold does not claim to include their source code or assets as-is.

## 3. Module integration policy

The project follows this rule:
- If a module is not fully verified, it remains in a planning or integrating state.
- No module is described as tested or offline-ready unless it has passed relevant checks.
- Third-party code is not included without a review of licensing, provenance, and compatibility.

## 4. Required notices for future integrations

When any external model, dataset, or asset is added, include:
- name of asset or model
- source repository or provider
- license or terms of use
- version or commit hash used
- modification summary
- attribution and citation requirements
- offline caching policy and provenance record

## 5. License summary

This repository is licensed under the MIT License unless a different license is added for a future integrated component. Any third-party component added later must preserve the original license notices and must not be redistributed in a way that violates the upstream terms.
